    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39925" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quā^drŭpĕdus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quā^drĭpĕdus</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Front. ad M. Anton. Or. 1</span></i>), a,
		um, adj.
		quadrupes, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>going on four feet</i>, <i>galloping</i> (postAug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quadrupedo gradu repentes,</span>”
				<i>on all fours</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 14, 2, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quadripedo cursu,</span>”
				<i>on a gallop</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Front.
					1, 1</span></i>
			.— <b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quadrupedo currere,</span>”
				<i>to gallop</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Front. Ep. ad M. Caes. 2, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
